TEXT 160 0 Left 3 ;#161 The same probe shown demodulating an AM carrier
TEXT 160 64 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C8SKiyJUAlU
TEXT 160 112 Left 2 ;With an amplitude-modulated carrier at the tip, the detector output follows the envelope,
TEXT 160 144 Left 2 ;which is the last of the four uses Alan lists on his notes page.
TEXT 1230 256 Left 2 !.lib ..\..\LTspice\Models\Unverified\1N34A_legacy.lib
TEXT 1230 296 Left 2 !.param VRMS=1 VPK={VRMS*sqrt(2)} MDEPTH=0.5 FMOD=20k FCAR=1Meg
TEXT 1230 376 Left 2 !.tran 0 400u 200u 5n
TEXT 1230 416 Left 2 !.meas tran VDET_AVG AVG V(detected) FROM 200u TO 400u
TEXT 1230 456 Left 2 !.meas tran VDET_MAX MAX V(detected) FROM 200u TO 400u
TEXT 1230 496 Left 2 !.meas tran VDET_MIN MIN V(detected) FROM 200u TO 400u
TEXT 160 680 Left 2 ;Alan's notes give the whole circuit: two 1N34A, two 1 nF and 10 kohm, useful from about
TEXT 160 712 Left 2 ;100 kHz to 100 MHz. The 1 MHz drive is a choice inside that range; his own calibration
TEXT 160 744 Left 2 ;curve is plotted against the RF input in volts RMS. Here VRMS is held at 1 V and modulated.
TEXT 160 792 Left 2 ;The 1N34A model is a legacy germanium fit of unverified provenance, not a manufacturer part.
TEXT 160 840 Left 2 ;BRF is a behavioural source standing in for the generator AM mode: 1 MHz carrier, 20 kHz tone,
TEXT 160 872 Left 2 ;50 percent depth. Alan does not state his own carrier or tone, so all three are choices here.
TEXT 1230 576 Left 2 ;BRF value, hidden on the symbol because the string is long:
TEXT 1230 608 Left 2 ;V={VPK*(1+MDEPTH*sin(2*pi*FMOD*time))*sin(2*pi*FCAR*time)}
